<title>CHINA: Bank of China profits 11.6 billion yuan in 1996.</title>
<headline>Bank of China profits 11.6 billion yuan in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of China, one of China's four big state-run commercial banks, generated 11.6 billion yuan ($1.39 billion) in profits in 1996, the Xinhua news agency said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bank's total assets were valued at 2.1 trillion yuan at the end of last year, Xinhua quoted Jiang Zuqi, vice-president of the bank, as saying.</p>
<p>Total assets of the bank's overseas branches reached $131 billion at the end of 1996, Jiang said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
